    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-16T04:10:53+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-16T04:10:53+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-15T18:40:53Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-15T18:40:53Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system southeast of the state slowly drifts further to the southeast over Tasmania today and is forecast to be located in the Tasman Sea on Monday, while extending a ridge over much of South Australia through to Tuesday. A trough of low pressure over Queensland pushes into the far northeast of SA until Monday, as another trough moves into far southwestern parts later on Tuesday and moves southeast across the state into Wednesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW011" description="Eastern Eyre Peninsula" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-16T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-17T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-15T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-16T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a light shower, becoming less likely in the late morning. Light winds becoming easterly 15 to 20 km/h in the morning then tending southeasterly in the late afternoon. Daytime maximum temperatures around 15.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 10:30am to 2:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 4 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-08-17T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-16T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Winds east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h turning northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the late morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 9 with daytime temperatures reaching around 17.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-19T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-18T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the afternoon and evening. Winds northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h turning northerly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 10 with daytime temperatures reaching around 20.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-08-19T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-20T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-18T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-19T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the evening. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds northwesterly 15 to 25 km/h becoming light during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 23.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
